# @PORT_TITLE@

A port of @PORT_TITLE@ on XenoForge's SDK: the game's code recompiled ahead of
time from your own disc and linked with XenoForge's runtime (kernel, GPU,
sound, input), with this repository's own code on top. No part of the game is
in the repository: the build reads your disc image.

## Building

You need XenoForge's SDK installed (`cmake --install <XenoForge's build>
--component sdk --prefix <dir>`), clang, CMake 3.25+ and Ninja.

```
cmake --preset default -DXENOFORGE_SDK=<the SDK's prefix> -DGAME_ISO=<your disc image>
cmake --build --preset default
```

(or `cmake --preset local` and `cmake --build --preset local`, with the paths
in `CMakeUserPresets.json`, which is not versioned). The first build
recompiles the disc: several minutes.

## Running

```
build/player_@PORT_NAME@ <disc image>                 # the game in a window
build/boot_@PORT_NAME@ <disc image> --seconds 20      # headless, with a report
```

Both take XenoForge's usual command line (its `docs/runtime.md`) and
`--option <key>=<value>` for this port's options.

## Layout

| path | what |
|---|---|
| `src/main.cpp` | the port's main: its name, options, `on_init` |
| `src/hooks.cpp` | hooks on the game's functions, reloaded while it runs |
| `project.toml` | the recompiler's project file: names, hooked functions, fixes to discovery |
